## Usage

### Basic Usage

```razor
<QuickGrid Items="@items" Class="qg-grid">
    <PropertyColumn Property="@(x => x.Name)" />
    <PropertyColumn Property="@(x => x.Email)" />
    
    <RowColumn TGridItem="Person" 
               ExpandedRowSpan="3"
               RowHeight="48"
               ExpandButtonText="Edit">
        <ExpandedTemplate Context="ctx">
            <RowCard Title="Details" OnClose="ctx.CollapseAsync">
                <ChildContent>
                    <p>Name: @ctx.Item.Name</p>
                    <p>Email: @ctx.Item.Email</p>
                </ChildContent>
                <FooterContent>
                    <button @onclick="ctx.CollapseAsync">Close</button>
                </FooterContent>
            </RowCard>
        </ExpandedTemplate>
    </RowColumn>
</QuickGrid>
```

### Custom Display Template

```razor
<RowColumn TGridItem="Person" TriggerMode="RowTriggerMode.Custom">
    <DisplayTemplate Context="ctx">
        <button class="qg-btn qg-btn-primary qg-btn-sm" 
                @onclick="ctx.ExpandAsync"
                disabled="@(!ctx.CanExpand)">
            <i class="bi bi-eye"></i> View
        </button>
    </DisplayTemplate>
    <ExpandedTemplate Context="ctx">
        <RowCard Title="Person Details" OnClose="ctx.CollapseAsync">
            <!-- Content -->
        </RowCard>
    </ExpandedTemplate>
</RowColumn>
```

### Multiple Rows Expanded

```razor
<RowColumn TGridItem="Person"
           ConcurrentBehavior="ConcurrentExpandBehavior.AllowMultiple"
           DimInactiveRows="false"
           ExpandedRowSpan="2">
    <ExpandedTemplate Context="ctx">
        <!-- Content -->
    </ExpandedTemplate>
</RowColumn>
```

## Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
|-----------|------|---------|-------------|
| `TriggerMode` | `RowTriggerMode` | `Button` | How expand is triggered |
| `ConcurrentBehavior` | `ConcurrentExpandBehavior` | `Block` | Multi-row behavior |
| `DimInactiveRows` | `bool` | `true` | Dim non-expanded rows |
| `ExpandedRowSpan` | `int` | `3` | Number of row heights the card spans |
| `RowHeight` | `int` | `48` | Height of each row in pixels |
| `DisplayTemplate` | `RenderFragment<RowDisplayContext>` | null | Collapsed state content |
| `ExpandedTemplate` | `RenderFragment<RowExpandedContext>` | **Required** | Expanded state content |
| `ExpandButtonText` | `string` | `"Edit"` | Button text |
| `ExpandButtonClass` | `string` | `"qg-btn..."` | Button CSS class |
| `ExpandButtonIcon` | `string?` | `"bi bi-pencil"` | Button icon class |

## Row Spanning for Virtualization

For QuickGrid virtualization compatibility, all rows must have uniform height. The `ExpandedRowSpan` and `RowHeight` parameters work together:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Row 1 (Expanded)  [Edit]                            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════╗   │  ─┐
│ ║  Expanded Card Content                        ║   │   │
│ ║  Height = ExpandedRowSpan × RowHeight         ║   │   ├─ 3 rows × 48px = 144px
│ ║  (3 × 48 = 144px)                             ║   │   │
│ ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════╝   │  ─┘
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Row 2 (covered by card)                             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Row 3 (covered by card)                             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Row 4 (visible below card)                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Events

| Event | Args | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `OnBeforeExpand` | `RowBeforeExpandEventArgs` | Before expand (cancellable) |
| `OnExpanded` | `RowExpandedEventArgs` | After row expanded |
| `OnCollapsed` | `RowCollapsedEventArgs` | After row collapsed |
| `OnStateChanged` | `RowStateChangedEventArgs` | Any state transition |

## Derived Classes

`RowColumn` is designed to be extended. Key virtual methods:

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `OnEnteringExpandedModeAsync(item)` | Set up state before row expands (e.g., create draft) |
| `OnExitingExpandedModeAsync(item)` | Clean up before row collapses (e.g., discard draft) |
| `ExpandRowAsync(item)` | Override to customize expand behavior |
| `CollapseRowAsync(item)` | Override to customize collapse behavior |

### Example: FormRowColumn (Derived)

```csharp
public class FormRowColumn<TGridItem> : RowColumn<TGridItem>
{
    protected override async Task OnEnteringExpandedModeAsync(TGridItem item)
    {
        // Create draft state for editing
        _draftManager.CreateDraft(item);
    }

    protected override async Task OnExitingExpandedModeAsync(TGridItem item)
    {
        // Discard draft if cancelled
        _draftManager.DiscardDraft(item);
    }
}
```

